*** 9 Additial inputs for impurity transport                 
*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
* 18.03.2013: Extension to multi impurity species
* Each impurity species specified in the ion sepcies table in input.par needs 
* own IMPUT.IMP_I file where the last integer I is the inpurity sepcies index.
* For example, if there are C and Fe two impurities listed in input.par with
* index 2 and 3, respectively, two input files, i.e. INPUT.IMP_2 and INPUT.IMP_3
* must be prepared for C and Fe separately.
*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
** 9.1 Transport model
* default IMPUTRIY_MOD=0: no impuries, neither transport no radiation
*                     <0: Coronal Equilibrium for radiation in ENERGY
*                      1: trace impurity fluid -- present version
*                      2: kinetic model to be developed
*                      3: coupled with other codes (not yet available)
1   
** 9.2 atomic-process Database
*STRAHL, ADAS, USER(not yet available) 
*---------1.  STRAHL ------------------------------------------
* In case of using STRAHL database, you need simply to put the| 
* keyword 'STRAHL' bellow. At the same time, the file 'STRAHL'|
* containing the atomic data must be provided.                |
*---------2. ADAS ---------------------------------------------
* Data block structure for using ADAS                         |
* ADAS      ! keyword                                         |
* NFILE     ! totoal number of adas data files                |
* PATH&files, where a class name like 'scd','acd' .... must   |
* appear at least once for classifying the preocesses.        |
* for example:                                                |
* ADAS      ! Call ADAS database                              | 
* 3         ! 3 totoal processes                              |
*/afs/ipp/u/adas/adas/adf11/scd96/scd96_c.dat                 |
*/afs/ipp/u/adas/adas/adf11/acd96/acd96_c.dat                 |
*/afs/ipp/u/adas/adas/adf11/plt96/plt96_c.dat                 |
*---------3. USER supplied ------------------------------------
